 @BrocKelley  Maybe, but I wouldn't be so sure. I will be extremely surprised if the 3070 is actually anywhere near the performance Nvidia claimed. It's obvious they drastically over promised with the 3080. 
I also wouldn't be so sure these prices are going to stay as low as they are now. Remember the 2080 To was supposed to be $999, but it never actually sold for anything less than $1200 after launch day. I think the only thing that could keep the current pricing in check is a competitive Big Nave, but that us yet to be seen. 
But all of that stuff that may happen in the future is just speculation. My main point is that people bought into the hype put forth by Nvidia, jumped the gun and started selling 2080Ti's in droves, tanking the price, then couldn't get a 3080 when they wanted to because bots bought them all up. Now the 3080's are all being sold on eBay for over $1000 and 2080Ti's are back up to $900. The exact same thing happened to 1080Ti's when RTX launched. The price tanked following Jensen's reveal full of unrealistic claims, then when reviews came out showing there was no price to performance increase, 1080Ti's went back up to around $700 and stayed there for 2 years.

